<div class="container">
    <h1 class="doc-h1">Changelog 2026-08-17 — Hermes Branch Context system</h1>

    <div class="last-updated" doc-muted>
        Last Updated: 2026-08-17 | Version: 0.1 | Tracked in project:
        <a href="/project/details?project_id=238" class="doc-link">#238 (GITWT-NEW)</a>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">What changed</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Branch <code>.hermes.md</code> domain files</strong> written for the 6 existing worktrees: InventoryAccounting (SQL-Ledger/Postgres &#8644; MySQL inventory posting contract), 3d (printing_3d consuming inventory / feeding accounting), DockerHA (K3s/HA + immutable-image deploy), ai (v2 AI chat + agents), aichatsystem-ef4e (legacy AIChat spec), git (worktree system itself). Each re-includes the global <code>/home/shanta/PycharmProjects/comserv2/.hermes.md</code> then adds domain expertise. BMaster (beekeeping) deferred until its worktree exists.</li>
                <li><strong>Git dashboard "Hermes" button</strong> — <code>Util/Git.pm -&gt; build_worktree_list</code> emits <code>hermes_cmd</code> (<code>cd &lt;worktree-git-root&gt; &amp;&amp; hermes chat -w</code>); <code>root/admin/git/index.tt</code> adds the button (and fixes Open to use an absolute <code>scheme://host:port/path</code> URL); <code>root/static/js/git-dashboard.js</code> copies the command to clipboard + shows it in the dev console.</li>
                <li><strong>Planning plan doc</strong> — <a href="/Documentation/HermesBranchContextPlan" class="doc-link">/Documentation/HermesBranchContextPlan</a>, tracked under #238 with todos 2142–2146 (2146 recurring re-audit, set recurrence in the Todo UI).</li>
                <li><strong>MASTER_PLAN</strong> — new index row + "Hermes Context" navlink; back-links added from the three sibling git-worktree plans.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="doc-h2">Why</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Each worktree is its own git root, so Hermes does not inherit the repo-root global rules. Without per-branch <code>.hermes.md</code>, a branch session silently loses writing styles, naming, and API rules. The button gives a one-click path from the app to an isolated, branch-aware Hermes.</p>

